# Agent quality gate (CI parity)

Human commits may skip hooks. **Agent-authored code must pass the same gates as `.github/workflows/quality.yml` before the task is done.**

## When

- After substantive edits to code under `web/`, `lambdas/`, `packages/`, or `infrastructure/`
- **Not** mid-turn while still exploring or iterating with the user — run once at the end of the change set (or before declaring done / opening a PR)
- Skip only for pure docs/config with no code impact, or when the user explicitly says to skip checks

## What (match CI)

For each **touched package** (directory with its own justfile), run:

1. `just fmt` then verify with `fmt-check` (or format then check)
2. `just lint` (auto-fix) then `lint-check`
3. `just typecheck`
4. `just test` when tests exist and the change can affect behavior

Prefer package-scoped commands:

```text
just --justfile <pkg>/justfile --working-directory <pkg> <recipe>
```

Use root `just check` only when many packages changed or selective scope is unclear.

## Conscious scope

- Map changed files → package roots; only check those packages
- If a shared package changed (`packages/*`), also typecheck/test direct dependents you edited in the same task
- State briefly which packages you checked (or why you skipped)

## Don't

- Treat “looks fine” or editor diagnostics alone as enough
- Leave ruff/ty failures for CI
- Skip because checks are slow — run them; fix failures before finishing
